# Two failure modes of single-quoted predicate values, which go through the FEA
# lexer token by token (unlike glyphsLib's opaque regex capture, and unlike a
# double-quoted value, which is one String lexeme):
#
# 1. An unterminated quote: the value scanner stops at `]`, so the damage stays
#    local -- one error, and the NEXT statement must parse clean (that is what
#    the second class below asserts).
# 2. A `#` inside the quotes starts a FEA comment that swallows the closing
#    quote, brackets and semicolon, cascading one error per enclosing construct
#    to EOF. This is the divergence documented at the top of the predicate
#    grammar in parse/grammar/glyph.rs. It must stay LAST in this file (and in
#    a file of its own, separate from glyphsapp_predicate_bad.fea, which ends
#    with its own at-EOF case): everything after it would be swallowed too.
@single_quote_recovery = [$[name == 'x] B];
@after_single_quote_recovery = [C];
@single_quote_comment = [$[name == 'a #the comment consumes the closing quote and brackets ']];
